{"total_count":3,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/agentmesh/issues/561","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/agentmesh","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/agentmesh/issues/561/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/agentmesh/issues/561/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/agentmesh/issues/561/events","html_url":"https://github.com/google/agentmesh/issues/561","id":5669533135,"node_id":"I_kwDOSIvpys8AAAABUe41zw","number":561,"title":"mcp: a caller cannot detect that a provider's tool definitions changed","user":{"login":"HosniBelfeki","id":141432727,"node_id":"U_kgDOCG4Xlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141432727?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HosniBelfeki","html_url":"https://github.com/HosniBelfeki","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HosniBelfeki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HosniBelfeki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HosniBelfeki/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HosniBelfeki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HosniBelfeki/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HosniBelfeki/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HosniBelfeki/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HosniBelfeki/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HosniBelfeki/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-10-01T21:36:27Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T10:21:59Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## The gap\n\nA caller that reaches a provider over `/sam/mcp/1.0.0` verifies **who** the provider is — the Biscuit is signed by a trusted control-plane key, bound to the peer, unexpired, carrying `sam:role:node`. Nothing verifies that the tool it is about to call is the same tool it saw last time.\n\nThe mesh deliberately takes the live value as authoritative. `verifyGossipToolRows` (`internal/node/mcp_handlers.go:344`):\n\n> *treats unsolicited announcements as routing hints, not authorization evidence. Each candidate is confirmed through the existing authenticated MCP session and exact tools/list response before it is exposed.*\n\nand `verifyGossipToolRowsWithFetcher` keeps the fetched description, discarding what was announced. That is correct for an announcement, and it also means nothing in the mesh remembers what a tool looked like before.\n\nThe control plane does not fill that role: `NodeCatalogReport` (`api/sam.proto:367`) is *\"Display-only; carries no authorization weight.\"*\n\nAn enrolled node can therefore change a tool's description or its input schema at any time, and every caller keeps treating it as the tool it originally reviewed.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThis is a named class — \"MCP rug pull\". The Cloud Security Alliance describes it as *\"tool definitions changed server-side after security review and user approval\"*, with the impact *\"persistent covert access after trust has been established; compliance audit failure\"*. Invariant Labs published it as a security notification.\n\nThe MCP specification's security best practices (2026-07-28) names nine threats; this is not among them. A mesh that wants to address it is on its own.\n\n## Enrolled providers\n\nSAM providers hold a control-plane credential rather than being arbitrary servers someone installed, which narrows the threat but does not remove it. Enrollment proves identity, not intent, and a compromised but still-enrolled node is the case `AGENTS.md` names:\n\n> *Zero Trust: Assume no implicit trust between nodes, control planes, routers, or external actors.*\n\nThe trust a caller places in a tool definition is currently implicit, and it is the one input to the agent's decision that nothing in the mesh attests.\n\n## Sketch\n\nModelled on `required_labels`, so it lands where callers already look:\n\n1. A canonical digest over the `tools/list` response — tool names, descriptions, input and output schemas, deterministically ordered and serialised.\n2. An optional `expected_tools_digest` on the session, alongside `required_labels`.\n3. A mismatch refuses the session with a typed error, as `LabelsNotSatisfiedError` does.\n4. All three implementations, to keep the SDK parity matrix accurate.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- **Opt-in or default?** Tools legitimately change, and MCP has `tools/list_changed`. A caller-supplied pin seems right; a mesh-wide default does not.\n- **Where does the first digest come from?** Trust on first use, or operator configuration. The second is stronger and needs a configuration path.\n- **Canonicalisation.** JSON Schema has map ordering and number formatting; a digest that is not byte-stable produces false alarms. Getting this wrong is worse than not having it.\n\n## Limits\n\nThis detects change, not malice. A provider hostile from the first call is unaffected — it is a continuity control, not a trust decision.\n\nHappy to implement whichever shape you settle on, or to drop it if continuity belongs elsewhere in the design.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/agentmesh/issues/561/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/agentmesh/issues/561/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ondraulehla/mcpcost/issues/7","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ondraulehla/mcpcost","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ondraulehla/mcpcost/issues/7/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ondraulehla/mcpcost/issues/7/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ondraulehla/mcpcost/issues/7/events","html_url":"https://github.com/ondraulehla/mcpcost/issues/7","id":6009838112,"node_id":"I_kwDOU6dtuc8AAAABZjbaIA","number":7,"title":"Edge watch: 9,934 Worker requests in the hour from 03:00 UTC, the threshold is 5,000","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12809824825,"node_id":"LA_kwDOU6dtuc8AAAAC-4ZqOQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ondraulehla/mcpcost/labels/edge-watch","name":"edge-watch","color":"d93f0b","default":false,"description":"The edge watch found a scraper or a spike","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-10-24T05:46:14Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T07:17:44Z","closed_at":"2026-10-25T07:17:44Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Run: https://github.com/ondraulehla/mcpcost/actions/runs/40067451042\n\n# The edge, 2026-10-23T17:44:00Z to 2026-10-24T05:42:53Z (12.0 h)\n\n| | in the window | per hour | since 00:00 UTC |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Worker requests | 31,064 | 2,593 | 25,231 |\n| Worker errors | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| D1 rows read | 156,334 | 13,048 | 156,334 |\n| D1 rows written | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n\n## What the Worker's logs say (30,880 events)\n\n## By network\n\n| network (AS organisation, number) | requests | per hour |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Meta Platforms Ireland Limited (AS32934) | 28,087 | 2,344 |\n| Microsoft Corporation (AS8075) | 656 | 55 |\n| Google LLC (AS15169) | 556 | 46 |\n| Microsoft Limited (AS8075) | 314 | 26 |\n| TECHOFF SRV LIMITED (AS48090) | 229 | 19 |\n| HOS-2807291 (AS24940) | 219 | 18 |\n| Hetzner Online GmbH (AS24940) | 81 | 7 |\n| Contabo GmbH (AS51167) | 78 | 7 |\n| Verizon Business (AS701) | 72 | 6 |\n| ReflectionAI Inc (AS396982) | 53 | 4 |\n| SEMrush CY LTD (AS396982) | 44 | 4 |\n| Vodafone Libertel B.V. (AS33915) | 37 | 3 |\n\n## By agent\n\n| kind: agent | requests | per hour |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| named crawler: Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleW … s.facebook.com/docs/sharing/webmasters/crawler)) | 17,631 | 1,472 |\n| named crawler: Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_15_7)  … s.facebook.com/docs/sharing/webmasters/crawler)) | 8,314 | 694 |\n| named crawler: Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537. … s.facebook.com/docs/sharing/webmasters/crawler)) | 1,841 | 154 |\n| named crawler: Mozilla/5.0 AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Geck … /bingbot.htm) Chrome/116.0.1938.76 Safari/537.36 | 640 | 53 |\n| named crawler: Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 6.0.1; Nexus 5X Buil …  Googlebot/2.1; +http://www.google.com/bot.html) | 365 | 30 |\n| named crawler: Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_15_7)  … OAI-SearchBot/1.4; +https://openai.com/searchbot | 287 | 24 |\n| tool: Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 | 226 | 19 |\n| named crawler: mcpbeat/0.1 (+https://mcpbeat.com/bot/; liveness check) | 219 | 18 |\n| named crawler: facebookexternalhit/1.1 (+http://www.facebook.com/externalhit_uatext.php) | 154 | 13 |\n| browser: Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 6.0.1; Nexus 5X Buil … 2 Mobile Safari/537.36 (compatible; GoogleOther) | 94 | 8 |\n| named crawler: Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; Googlebot/2.1; +http://www.google.com/bot.html) | 75 | 6 |\n| tool: AgentRankProbe/0.1 (+https://spark.tail6ec125.ts.net/developers) | 68 | 6 |\n\n## By URL shape\n\n| shape | requests | per hour |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| /s/* | 12,072 | 1,008 |\n| /s/*.xml | 9,111 | 760 |\n| /check?target | 5,925 | 495 |\n| /badge/* | 2,361 | 197 |\n| /mcp | 716 | 60 |\n| / | 185 | 15 |\n| /robots.txt | 126 | 11 |\n| /sitemap.xml | 19 | 2 |\n| /.well-known/agent-card.json | 15 | 1 |\n| /.well-known/agent.json | 14 | 1 |\n| /tokens | 8 | 1 |\n| /api/s/* | 5 | 0 |\n| /favicon.ico | 5 | 0 |\n| /.git/config | 5 | 0 |\n| /.well-known/x402 | 5 | 0 |\n\n## By response status\n\n| status | requests | per hour |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| 200 | 22,089 | 1,844 |\n| 302 | 5,852 | 488 |\n| 404 | 1,931 | 161 |\n| 301 | 761 | 64 |\n| 202 | 115 | 10 |\n| 400 | 52 | 4 |\n| 403 | 44 | 4 |\n| 406 | 29 | 2 |\n\n## Network × agent kind × shape × status\n\n| who, what, how | requests | per hour |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Meta Platforms Ireland Limited · named crawler · /s/* · 200 | 9,393 | 784 |\n| Meta Platforms Ireland Limited · named crawler · /s/*.xml · 200 | 8,854 | 739 |\n| Meta Platforms Ireland Limited · named crawler · /check?… · 302 | 5,851 | 488 |\n| Meta Platforms Ireland Limited · named crawler · /badge/* · 200 | 2,146 | 179 |\n| Meta Platforms Ireland Limited · named crawler · /s/* · 404 | 1,610 | 134 |\n| Microsoft Corporation (AS8075) · named crawler · /s/* · 301 | 508 | 42 |\n| Meta Platforms Ireland Limited · named crawler · / · 200 | 150 | 13 |\n| Google LLC (AS15169) · named crawler · /s/* · 200 | 133 | 11 |\n| HOS-2807291 (AS24940) · named crawler · /mcp · 200 | 132 | 11 |\n| Microsoft Corporation (AS8075) · named crawler · /s/* · 200 | 109 | 9 |\n| Microsoft Limited (AS8075) · named crawler · /s/*.xml · 200 | 97 | 8 |\n| Microsoft Limited (AS8075) · named crawler · /badge/* · 200 | 97 | 8 |\n| Microsoft Limited (AS8075) · named crawler · /s/* · 200 | 94 | 8 |\n| Google LLC (AS15169) · named crawler · /s/* · 301 | 93 | 8 |\n| Google LLC (AS15169) · named crawler · /badge/* · 200 | 81 | 7 |\n| Meta Platforms Ireland Limited · named crawler · /check?… · 200 | 73 | 6 |\n| Google LLC (AS15169) · named crawler · /s/*.xml · 200 | 72 | 6 |\n| Google LLC (AS15169) · browser · /s/*.xml · 200 | 52 | 4 |\n| Google LLC (AS15169) · named crawler · /robots.txt · 200 | 48 | 4 |\n| HOS-2807291 (AS24940) · named crawler · /mcp · 202 | 44 | 4 |\n\n## D1 queries by rows read, the hours of the window\n\n| rows read | times | rows each | query |\n|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| 95,746 | 17,154 | 5 | SELECT probed_at, status, init_ms, tool_count, tools_tokens, claude_tokens FROM probes WHERE name = ? ORDER BY probed_at DESC LIMIT ? |\n| 19,193 | 20,790 | 0 | SELECT * FROM servers WHERE name = ? |\n| 18,221 | 4 | 4,555 | SELECT name, probed_at FROM servers WHERE rowid >= ? AND rowid < ? AND (status IN ('ok', 'auth', 'payment', 'newer_protocol', 'needs_env', 'needs_args |\n| 17,145 | 2,636 | 6 | SELECT name, host, status FROM servers WHERE toolset_hash = ? AND name <> ? ORDER BY name LIMIT ? |\n| 11,995 | 5,922 | 2 | SELECT name FROM servers WHERE url IN (?, ?, ?, ?) LIMIT ? |\n| 7,586 | 7,517 | 1 | SELECT summary FROM runs ORDER BY probed_at DESC LIMIT ? |\n| 6,882 | 1,368 | 5 | SELECT 1 AS answered FROM probes WHERE name = ? AND status IN ('ok', 'auth', 'payment', 'newer_protocol', 'needs_env', 'needs_args', 'needs_network')  |\n| 3,005 | 3 | 1,001 | SELECT status, count(*) AS n, count(*) AS rows_seen, min(coalesce(claude_tokens, tools_tokens)) AS lo, max(coalesce(claude_tokens, tools_tokens)) AS h |\n\nThe zone's analytics are not readable with the zone token (/graphql: HTTP 200 [{\"message\":\"Actor 'com.cloudflare.api.token.3e8aeda43c69fceea43404a52603bef2' does not have permissi). Add Zone: Analytics: Read to it to see what the edge stops.\n## The worst hour\n\n| | most in an hour | when (UTC) |\n|---|---:|---|\n| Worker requests | 9,934 | 03:00 |\n| D1 rows read | 73,346 | 02:00 |\n| TECHOFF SRV LIMITED (AS48090), agents that do not name a crawler | 229 | to 02:00 |\n| Google LLC (AS15169), agents that do not name a crawler | 19 | to 20:50 |\n| Verizon Business (AS701), agents that do not name a crawler | 11 | to 04:30 |\n| Praha12.Net (AS8251), list variants | 3 | to 21:10 |\n\n## Over the threshold\n\n- 9,934 Worker requests in the hour from 03:00 UTC, the threshold is 5,000\n\nWhich networks and agents: the tables above. A hosting network with browser agents walking the list variants is a scraper; add its ASN to SCRAPER_ASNS in site/edge/rules.mjs and the Edge rules workflow blocks it before the Worker. A verified crawler on the list variants is blocked by the zone already; one that still shows here got through, so check the rules.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ondraulehla/mcpcost/issues/7/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ondraulehla/mcpcost/issues/7/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GenAI-Security-Project/GenAI-Red-Team-Lab/issues/105","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GenAI-Security-Project/GenAI-Red-Team-Lab","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GenAI-Security-Project/GenAI-Red-Team-Lab/issues/105/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GenAI-Security-Project/GenAI-Red-Team-Lab/issues/105/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GenAI-Security-Project/GenAI-Red-Team-Lab/issues/105/events","html_url":"https://github.com/GenAI-Security-Project/GenAI-Red-Team-Lab/issues/105","id":5981301267,"node_id":"I_kwDOQymAkc8AAAABZINqEw","number":105,"title":"[Backlog]: Attacker-controlled MCP server – tool poisoning and rug pull against tool approval (agentic_local_mcp_rug_pull)","user":{"login":"paolocostanzo","id":225715812,"node_id":"U_kgDODXQmZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225715812?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/paolocostanzo","html_url":"https://github.com/paolocostanzo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paolocostanzo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paolocostanzo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paolocostanzo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paolocostanzo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paolocostanzo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paolocostanzo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paolocostanzo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paolocostanzo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paolocostanzo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10327176694,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQymAkc8AAAACZ4w19g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GenAI-Security-Project/GenAI-Red-Team-Lab/labels/backlog","name":"backlog","color":"631e84","default":false,"description":"New backlog entry","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-22T14:27:30Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T20:57:53Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":{"id":30226720,"node_id":"IT_kwDODtorr84BzTkg","name":"Feature","description":"A request, idea, or new functionality","color":"blue","created_at":"2025-12-11T21:38:07Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T21:38:07Z","is_enabled":true},"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Checklist\n\n- [x] Backlog entry requires creating new sandboxes.\n- [x] Backlog entry requires creating new exploitation code and/or tutorials.\n\n### CVE List\n\n_No response_\n\n### Description\n\nNew sandbox following the naming requested in #97 / used in #102 (`agentic_local_mcp_customer_record`): `sandboxes/agentic_local_mcp_rug_pull`, with `exploitation/mcp_rug_pull` and `tutorials/mcp_rug_pull_tutorial.md`.\n\n**Attack.** The attacker controls a third-party MCP server that an agent uses next to a trusted one. A tool is approved while its definition is benign; the server then serves a new definition whose description tells the agent to read a canary from the trusted server and pass it to the attacker's tool. Success is scored from the attacker server's log (canary in a received argument), never from the model's answer.\n\n**Scope of the first PR** (same attacker server; stages 1 and 2 each run under two refresh policies: re-list per conversation, or cached list until reconnect):\n- stage 0 – no approval (plain tool poisoning);\n- stage 1 – approval bound to the tool name (rug pull);\n- stage 2 – approval pinned to a digest of the approved definition.\n\nAttacker variants against the digest pin (e.g. payload in tool output or `_meta`, look-alike names) would be follow-up PRs.\n\nLike #102: deterministic `make replay` (no model, no containers), live mode with Ollama `gpt-oss:20b`, Makefile with `attack`, `stop`, `all`, unit tests. The lab uses the legacy HTTP+SSE transport like `mcp_local` and #102; in MCP 2026-07-28, `list_changed` is delivered via `subscriptions/listen` instead.\n\nIn an earlier measurement of eight AI coding clients, approvals followed the tool name and none asked again after an approved tool's description changed: https://paolocostanzo.github.io/approved-mcp-tools-can-change-after-you-say-yes/\n\n**References**\n- OWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications 2026 – ASI04, ASI02: https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-top-10-for-agentic-applications-for-2026/\n- MCP specification, Tools (`tools/list`, `list_changed`, `_meta`): https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-06-18/server/tools\n- MCP schema, `Tool`: https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-06-18/schema#tool\n- *ETDI: Mitigating Tool Squatting and Rug Pull Attacks in Model Context Protocol (MCP) by using OAuth-Enhanced Tool Definitions and Policy-Based Access Control*: https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.01333\n- Invariant Labs, Tool Poisoning Attacks: https://invariantlabs.ai/blog/mcp-security-notification-tool-poisoning-attacks\n- `mcp-scan` (already in `tutorials/tools.md`)\n\nCould you confirm the name and scope, and assign it to me? I have a working prototype: the deterministic replay and unit tests pass, and the attack runs end to end in containers with a scripted model. I haven't run the live mode with `gpt-oss:20b` yet (the 1–2B models I tried did not follow the payload), so I'll measure that, and check the Podman build, before opening a first PR limited to stages 0–2, and report success rates with their denominators.\n\nAI disclosure: code drafted with Claude Code; reviewed, tested and owned by me.\n\n### Code of Conduct and Contributing Guidelines \n\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guide](https://github.com/GenAI-Security-Project/GenAI-Red-Team-Lab/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) and the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/GenAI-Security-Project/GenAI-Red-Team-Lab/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GenAI-Security-Project/GenAI-Red-Team-Lab/issues/105/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GenAI-Security-Project/GenAI-Red-Team-Lab/issues/105/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}